WEBVTT

NOTE The Commons, episode 01. Same words as the captions in the picture.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
[Music]

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.750
Thirty-one years I ran the night shift.

3
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.250
Lorries out the door before the sun was up.

4
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.250
Then one Tuesday, they thanked me for my service.

5
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.750
So I dug out my CV. It was in the loft.

6
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.600
On a floppy disk.

7
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.750
Our Zara looked at it like it was a fossil.

8
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.750
“Nan, nothing can even open that.”

9
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.750
We got it open. Purple.

10
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.750
Comic Sans. A photo of me in shoulder pads.

11
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.750
Zara had to have a lie down.

12
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.500
Her advice?

13
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.600
Stop listing duties. Say what you actually did.

14
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:50.000
Two pages, plain font, every word earning its place.

15
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:56.250
Turns out thirty-one years of keeping the lights on is exactly what they were after.

16
00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:02.500
If your CV’s older than your grandkids, there’s a free guide for that. Come on.

17
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:09.500
[Music]
